{"type": "thinking", "text": "Hmm, after Show answer, nothing changed—still displays only \"The front of this card is blank.\" That may be normal for a blank card (backside also blank?). Actually with optional reversed card empty, Card 2's question side is {{#Add Reverse}}...{{/Add Reverse}}, blank. Answer side would be {{FrontSide}} + back maybe also blank. So it shows blank side. Hmm, but \"The front of this card is blank.\" persists in answer view. Might be expected behavior of AnkiDroid for empty card. Let me not report yet.\n\nNow let's test the more suspicious changed behavior: \"preview pages are now indexed directly by each card's template position\". Consider a note type where card templates are conditionally generated and ordering. For example, a note type with 2 templates where card 2 is not generated (optional reverse): tab label \"Card 2 (empty)\" indicates they consider template 2 empty. Fine.\n\nWhat about Cloze? Cloze note type has one template \"Cloze\", but multiple cards c1, c2. Preview in Add note: previously, for cloze, preview pages might be generated per card (c1, c2...). Now indexed by template position means only one preview page? Let me test Cloze with two clozes: text \"{{c1::one}} and {{c2::two}}\". Expect preview to show both cards (Card 1, Card 2?) with labels maybe \"Card 1\" and \"Card 2\". If indexed by template position, maybe both tabs map to index 0 of templates (only one template), showing same cloze card (c1) twice → bug.\n\nLet me test. Back, change type to Cloze, input cloze text."}
