rayed for cloze?), \"Delete Card Type\". Hmm.\n\nRather than guessing, maybe test functionality: tap \"Add card type\" on Cloze. If it really adds a second card type (which cloze doesn't support) or errors, that's a clear bug. But careful: we shouldn't change data unnecessarily; adding card type then undoing is okay if reversible. But risk corrupting deck. Could tap and then discard via back without save.\n\nAlternatively, test menu differences across models might be intended by change. Look at \"Deck override (off)\" missing for Cloze and Image Occlusion. In AnkiDroid, deck override is available for all note types? It's shown in Basic but not cloze. Hmm, maybe cloze doesn't show deck override. Actually deck override should be available for any note type. Hmm.\n\nLet me compare: Basic menu had 7 entries including \"Rename card type\" and \"Deck override (off)\". Cloze/IO have 5: Add card type, Browser appearance, Insert field, Copy as Markdown, Restore to default. Missing Rename card type and Deck override.\n\nMaybe correct behavior: For cloze note types (including Image Occlusion), \"Add card type\", \"Rename card type\", \"Deck override\" are hidden? But here Add card type is shown. Wait, maybe for cloze the correct is: rename hidden, add hidden, deck override shown? Hmm.\n\nLet me look at AnkiDroid source knowledge. In CardTemplateEditor.java (2.15/2.16):\n\n```java\n@Override\npublic boolean onPrepareOptionsMenu(Menu menu) {\n    menu.findItem(R.id.action_add_card_type).setVisible(mModel.getType() == Consts.MODEL_STD);\n    menu.findItem(R.id.action_rename_card_type).setVisible(...);\n    menu.findItem(R.id.action_deck_override).setVisible(...);\n    ...\n}\n```\n\nActually I recall in AnkiDroid, the template editor \"menu\" is built using `TemplateEditorViewModel`? Let me think of the changed line: \"the menu's entries are now built the same way for every kind of note model.\" A bug planted could be that the code builds menu using `model.getType()` comparisons incorrectly, e.g. for CLOZE it shows options intended for standard, and vice versa. The clear observable symptom: Cloze and Image Occlusion show \"Add card type\", which shouldn't be available because cloze notetypes only ever have one card type. Is that true? In Anki 2.1.28+, cloze note types can only have one card template — yes, adding a card type is not possible. Anki desktop: Cloze note type's card types list shows \"Cloze\" and \"Add Card Type\" is disabled? Hmm, actually I'm quite sure you cannot have multiple templates in a cloze notetype. So showing \"Add card type\" for Cloze is wrong.\n\nAlso \"Deck override\" missing for cloze might be wrong.\n\nTo confirm the outcome if clicked: if I tap \"Add card type\" for Cloze, does anything happen? Let's try: tap element 0. Then observe. If it adds \"Card 2\", that's definitely a bug (and reversible by delete/discard). Let's test."}
