{"type": "thinking", "text": "Basic (and reversed card) menu: Add card type, Reposition, Rename card type, Delete card type, Browser appearance, Deck override (off), Insert field, Copy as Markdown, Restore to default. That seems right for a standard note type with 2 templates.\n\nBasic (1 template) menu: Add card type, Rename card type, Browser appearance, Deck override (off), Insert field, Copy as Markdown, Restore to default. No Reposition/Delete since 1 template. Makes sense.\n\nCloze menu: Add card type, Browser appearance, Insert field, Copy as Markdown, Restore to default. Missing Rename, Deck override. Hmm, if \"built the same way for every kind of note model\", likely intended that the menu entries are consistent: Add card type should not be visible for cloze. Also Rename might be hidden for cloze because Anki doesn't allow renaming cloze template? And Deck override hidden? That seems odd but plausible if AnkiDroid's implementation uses \"isCloze\" to hide rename and deck override... no.\n\nLet me think about AnkiDroid's actual code (2.16 alpha). I recall `CardTemplateEditor` menu resource `card_template_editor.xml` has items: action_add_card_type, action_reposition, action_rename_card_type, action_delete_card_type, action_browser_appearance, action_deck_override, action_insert_field, action_copy_as_markdown, action_restore_default.\n\nIn onPrepareOptionsMenu (from memory of source):\n```java\nmenu.findItem(R.id.action_add_card_type).setVisible(!mModel.isCloze() || mModel.isImageOcclusion());\n```\nHmm not sure.\n\nAlternative: Maybe the actual bug is that menu entries are *duplicated*. Not here.\n\nWe need more evidence. Perhaps the developer planted bug is exactly something like: \"for Cloze/Image Occlusion, toolbar menu shows 'Add card type' which creates a second template and corrupts the note type\" — this would be caught by observing \"Add card type\" present. But is it truly wrong? Let's test in a safe way: proceed with Add on Cloze (there are 0 notes of Cloze type) and see if it creates \"Card 2\". If the backend rejects, nothing happens (maybe toast). If it succeeds, that indicates AnkiDroid allows multiple card types for cloze — which modern Anki may actually disallow at backend level, so success would be a bug. Then discard without saving, so no data changes persisted (we'll verify).\n\nActually, adding a card template to a note type with 0 notes is harmless and reversible via Delete card type (if available) or discard. Let's do it on Cloze. But wait, if it auto-saves on add? AnkiDroid's CardTemplateEditor applies changes when pressing Save (action_confirm). Actually in newer versions, changes are saved when you leave? There's a Save button. I'll discard.\n\nLet me do this test. Navigate back to manage note types, Cloze Edit cards, menu > Add card type > Add."}
