{"type": "thinking", "text": "It created \"Card 2\" for the Cloze note type, with template content \"{{cloze:Text}}<br>\\n{{Back Extra}}\". This is definitely suspicious: cloze note types cannot have multiple card templates in Anki. Is AnkiDroid supposed to prohibit this? In AnkiDroid's CardTemplateEditor, yes, cloze note types only have one card type. Historically, the \"Add card type\" menu item is hidden for cloze note types (AnkiDroid checks model type). So this created invalid state. This aligns with the changed build: menu entries built the same way for every model → Add wrongly shown for Cloze/Image Occlusion.\n\nBut wait — maybe modern AnkiDroid allows multiple templates for cloze? Let me think of AnkiDroid 2.17 source. I recall in CardTemplateEditor.java:\n\n```java\nprivate void updateOptionsMenu() {\n    mOptionsMenu.findItem(R.id.action_add_card_type).setVisible(mModel.getModel().getType() != Consts.MODEL_CLOZE);\n    ...\n}\n```\n\nHmm. Actually let me search memory: AnkiDroid has menu item \"action_add_card_type\" and code:\n```java\n@Override\npublic boolean onOptionsItemSelected(MenuItem item) {\n    int itemId = item.getItemId();\n    if (itemId == R.id.action_add_card_type) {\n        ...\n        int ordinal = getCardTypeOrdinal();\n```\nAnd visibility:\n```java\nmenu.findItem(R.id.action_add_card_type).setVisible(mModel.getType() == Consts.MODEL_STD);\n```\nI'm fairly confident the cloze type check exists somewhere. But the change note says entries are now built the same way for every kind of note model, which might be a refactor that dropped the type-specific visibility, causing Add card type to appear for cloze. This is likely the planted bug.\n\nHowever, there is also the possibility that the intended bug is that \"Rename card type\" and \"Deck override\" are missing for cloze/IO. Hmm. But with the menu unified, the code likely includes all items for all types... yet Rename/Deck override are absent for cloze. So the unification is partial: maybe the menu-building code is the same sequence but with `menu.findItem(...).setVisible(...)` conditions based on model type. The conditions produced:\n\n- Basic (std, 1 template): Add visible, Rename visible, [Reposition hidden, Delete hidden], Browser visible, Deck override visible.\n- Std 2 templates: all visible.\n- Cloze/IO: Add visible, Rename hidden, Reposition hidden, Delete hidden, Browser visible, Deck override hidden.\n\nHmm, that pattern could be intentional: for cloze, no rename (fixed name), no deck override? Deck override for cloze note types makes no sense? Actually deck override is per-note-type setting used to force cards into a deck; it works for cloze too. Hmm.\n\nWait, maybe Deck override requires that the model has a deck override property and the app hides it for cloze? Unlikely.\n\nLet me reconsider: maybe cloze note types' templates could be renamed in AnkiDroid but this build hides it incorrectly — that would be a bug \"Rename card type missing for Cloze\". But which is the intended planted bug? The change says \"the menu's entries are now built the same way for every kind of note model.\" If built the same way, all models should have the same entries (modulo applicability). The observed: Basic has 7, Cloze has 5, IO has 5. The difference could be intended by applicability: Add visible for all → wrong for cloze.\n\nAnother way: check a standard model created via \"Add note type\"? Not needed.\n\nLet's test whether creating Card 2 in Cloze breaks preview/saving. But first, is the created Card 2 persisted only in editor (unsaved)? Let's discard by back. If discard, we can't verify. But the bug is visible anyway.\n\nI should verify whether this \"Add card type\" behavior is truly wrong by checking if the app permits it in normal use. Consider: Anki's backend `add_card_template` actively rejects cloze notetypes: \"notetype is cloze\". Actually I recall in Anki's Rust backend, `Notetype::add_card_template` returns error \"cannot add card template to cloze notetype\". If so, AnkiDroid would show an error when saving (or adding), not silently create. That strongly suggests it's not allowed and the menu entry is a bug.\n\nLet me test saving this Card 2 to see the outcome: press Save. If it errors, that confirms backend rejects; but then we'd have an error message which is evidence. But careful: could corrupt? The save would fail and stay in editor. Let's try Save? Hmm, if backend allows (maybe AnkiDroid's backend permits), it would persist a cloze notetype with 2 templates and 0 notes — bad but we could delete again. Data change is minor and reversible.\n\nAlternatively, click Delete card type from menu now — but menu lacks Delete for cloze! Interesting: after adding Card 2, does Delete appear? Let me check menu now. If Delete is still missing, then we cannot remove Card 2 from the UI except discard — another bug. Let's open menu."}
