{"type": "thinking", "text": "Restored. Now decide on report for Cloze \"Add card type\".\n\nLet me verify against AnkiDroid's documented behavior. The known AnkiDroid feature: \"Card template editor\" menu. Search memory: AnkiDroid manual \"Card Templates\" — for cloze note types, the card template editor only shows one card type and the \"Add card type\" option is not shown. I am fairly confident.\n\nBut before filing, consider the exact change statement: \"Card template editor toolbar: the menu's entries are now built the same way for every kind of note model.\" The word \"toolbar\" — in Add Note screen, the formatting toolbar at bottom. Hmm! \"Card template editor toolbar\" — which toolbar? Card template editor has a toolbar at top with Save, Preview, More options. Menu entries built the same way for every kind of note model. \"Note model\" = note type. So maybe the change refers to the formatting toolbar (bold, italic, etc.) in the Card Template Editor's field editing? Hmm, no, \"menu's entries\" suggests overflow menu.\n\nActually \"the menu's entries are now built the same way for every kind of note model\" — the overflow menu of CardTemplateEditor. So our test is right.\n\nNow, what could be the planted bug? Perhaps duplicate entries. Let me check Basic (optional reversed card) and Basic (type in the answer) menus to see any missing/duplicated entries. Let me quickly cycle through all 6 types and record menus:\n\n- Basic (std, 1 template): Add, Rename, Browser, Deck override (off), Insert field, Copy as Markdown, Restore default. (7)\n- Basic (and reversed) (std, 2): Add, Reposition, Rename, Delete, Browser, Deck override (off), Insert field, Copy as Markdown, Restore default. (9)\n- Cloze (cloze, 1): Add, Browser, Insert field, Copy as Markdown, Restore default. (5)\n- Image Occlusion (cloze, 1): same 5.\n- Basic (optional reversed) (std, 2): probably same as and-reversed (9).\n- Basic (type in answer) (std, 1): same as Basic (7).\n\nHmm, the cloze missing Deck override may be intentional in AnkiDroid? Let me recall AnkiDroid code for `onPrepareOptionsMenu` in CardTemplateEditor 2.15:\n\nI found memory of a snippet:\n```java\n@Override\npublic boolean onPrepareOptionsMenu(Menu menu) {\n    super.onPrepareOptionsMenu(menu);\n    boolean addCardType = !mModel.isCloze();\n    menu.findItem(R.id.action_add_card_type).setVisible(addCardType);\n    ...\n}\n```\nNot certain.\n\nActually, I recall that in AnkiDroid, when editing a cloze note type's card template, the menu shows \"Add note type\"? no.\n\nLet me look at this from a different angle: maybe I can inspect the menu via UI differences on a *new* standard note type created with \"Add a new note type\" to compare. Not helpful.\n\nThe safest path: test the behavior that results from tapping \"Add card type\" on Cloze — it offers to add Card 2, creating an invalid cloze notetype. If that state is actually invalid, saving should fail. Let's test Save now? We reverted, so no changes. Hmm.\n\nAlternatively, test whether the created Card 2 for Cloze actually saves successfully, then check the Add Note screen's Type list (now \"Cloze\" with 2 cards) and preview. If saving succeeds, the app accepts multiple templates for a cloze type, which changes how cloze cards are generated? Anki backend's cloze card generation only creates cards based on cloze numbers, ignoring template ord > 0, so the second template would never generate cards — a dead template with 0 cards (\"This will create 0 cards\" indeed!). The dialog said \"This will create 0 cards\", suggesting the app knows Card 2 will never generate cards but allows it anyway (0 notes). That's consistent with adding a template to an empty notetype; for cloze it's still wrong because no note would ever produce cards for template 2.\n\nI think this is a legitimate bug: \"Add card type\" menu item is offered for Cloze and Image Occlusion note types, but cloze note types cannot use additional card templates (they only generate cards from cloze deletions), so the created 'Card 2' never creates cards. Expected: the option should be hidden/disabled for cloze-based note types.\n\nHowever, I'm not 100% sure Anki doesn't support multiple templates for cloze. Let me check via AnkiDroid UI after adding Card 2: if you add a cloze note, cards \"Cards: Cloze\" vs \"Card 2\"? In Add note screen, the \"Cards:\" button lists card types that would be generated? For a cloze note, cards list shows \"Cloze\" template. Adding a second template would mean cloze note cards would... Hmm.\n\nLet me test in a controlled way: Add Card 2 to Cloze, save, then go to Add note, select Cloze, enter cloze text and check \"Cards:\" and preview. If preview shows \"Card 2\" page empty, it's clearly broken. But this alters note type data (adds a template). We can delete it afterwards. Since Cloze has 0 notes, no card damage. It's within testing.\n\nActually, before that, maybe simpler: the bug might not be about Add-card-type at all. Let me re-read the change notes:\n\n1. \"Card preview from Add note: preview pages are now indexed directly by each card's template position.\" → found bug (cloze gaps).\n2. \"Card template editor toolbar: the menu's entries are now built the same way for every kind of note model.\" → likely a bug where menu entries differ wrongly between note types (e.g., cloze lacks \"Rename card type\"/\"Deck override\" while having \"Add card type\").\n3. \"Deck list expand/collapse arrows: a tap is now handled by redrawing only the affected deck's rows.\" → bug probably in deck list redraw: stale rows, wrong counts, etc. Need to test deck expand/collapse. But our deck list has no subdecks; maybe expanding a deck with children. Since no subdecks exist, expand arrows maybe not present. Hmm, but the change is specifically about collapse arrows in deck list. With two top decks and no children, no arrows. Maybe decks can be collapsed if they have subdecks; we might need to create a subdeck to test. The precondition says decks Spanish and French only. Maybe the deck list in this app version shows expand arrows for subdecks; none exist. Then we can't test unless we create a subdeck. Hmm, but maybe the deck list \"French\"/\"Spanish\" rows have a collapse arrow? Screenshot shows no arrow. So maybe the tested build's deck list is different (the deck picker in Add note shows \"French\", \"Spanish\" without arrows too). Hmm.\n\nWait — maybe the deck list refers to the deck overview / deck picker with nested decks? The change: \"Deck list expand/collapse arrows: a tap is now handled by redrawing only the affected deck's rows.\" In AnkiDroid deck list, when browsing the deck picker, there's a \"Deck list\" with arrows for decks with subdecks, controlled by \"Deck list\" prefs. Since there are no subdecks, we can create one to test. Creating a subdeck changes data (adds a deck), which may be acceptable \"Do not change data outside what testing requires\" — creating a subdeck is a test action; we could delete it afterwards. But risky? It's manageable.\n\n4. \"Manage note types: each type's note count is now computed in the background after the list appears.\" → bug likely: counts initially wrong, then update; maybe after rotation counts reset or a wrong count displayed (e.g., all showing 0, or stale). Let's test by adding a note then checking counts, rotating, etc.\n\nLet me continue with Manage note types counts thoroughly. Current state: Basic 7 notes. Let's go back to manage note types (we're in Cloze card types). Press back.\n\nTest plan for note counts:\n- Add a new Basic note to French (or Spanish), then return to Manage note types: Basic count should increase to 8. Check it (background computation might lag; wait).\n- Observe immediately on entry (list appears) — maybe count shows 0 then updates. Is transient 0 a bug? Probably not if updates quickly; but if a stale/wrong value persists, bug.\n- Rotate in Manage note types and check counts.\n- Check count consistency with deck list (Spanish 4 + French 3 = 7 Basic).\n\nAlso test \"Search\" maybe.\n\nLet me proceed."}
