{"type": "thinking", "text": "Counts: Basic 7 notes, Basic (and reversed card) 1 note (not 2 cards). Correct. Singular \"1 note\" grammar correct.\n\nNow, potential bug in background count: maybe counts are correct initially, but when returning to this screen after adding a note while it's in the back stack, counts might not update? We tested fresh entry. Let's test: open a note type's card types, back (returns to list) — counts correct. Another test: rotate back and forth after counts loaded — correct.\n\nMaybe the planted bug: counts computed in background after list appears, but if you leave before computation completes, a stale async update could set wrong counts on next visit? Hard to test.\n\nOr the bug: If a note type has notes and you open Manage note types, the count is briefly \"0 notes\" then updates. That's expected (background). But if the update fails for off-screen rows (only visible rows rebound), scrolling could show stale 0s. Let's scroll to Image Occlusion/Cloze — visible already; all counts correct.\n\nAnother possible bug: note counts are computed asynchronously and applied by list position, so if the list is re-sorted (via search) results mismatch. Test Search: tap Search and type \"Cloze\"? When filtered, rows shift; async count update might apply to wrong rows. Let's test search functionality with counts.\n\nTap Search (element 2)."}
