{"type": "thinking", "text": "Counts correct in landscape. Rotate back.\n\nNow test adding a new note type to see counts and menu. Actually, maybe first test the \"Basic (and reversed card)\" note deletion to see counts update correctly (Basic should 7, reversed 0 after deleting the note). Deleting via Card Browser is another route; but \"Do not change data outside what testing requires\" — we added qa_rev1, should clean up eventually. Deleting via Browser tests consistency too (deck list counts vs note types counts).\n\nBut maybe more efficient: we've verified counts consistent for 2 non-zero types. The planted bug might be that the count is *cards* not notes... we disproved (1 note vs 2 cards). Or that counts don't update until re-entry — we saw they do.\n\nWait, maybe the bug appears when one note type has notes in *both decks*: Basic has 7 across 2 decks — displayed 7. Correct. Hmm.\n\nMaybe the bug is with the \"Image Occlusion\" type: its note count computation in background might fail/crash? It shows 0 notes correctly.\n\nCould be a race: entering Manage note types right after adding a note shows stale count (cache). We saw correct 8 immediately after adding — because a new instance recomputes.\n\nHmm. Maybe the planted bug for Manage note types is different: The note count is computed in background **after the list appears**, and while that's happening, the list shows no counts / \"-\" briefly. But if the activity is recreated (rotation) while the count computation is in flight, counts might never appear (stuck). We rotated after counts loaded. Let's try rotating *immediately* after entering Manage note types (before counts finish). The counts may appear instantly though (fast). Hard to catch. But maybe we can induce slowness? Not easily.\n\nAlternatively, the bug could be that the background count updates are applied to *positions* in the filtered list, causing wrong counts shown when filtering. Test: filter \"reversed\" → showed 1 note/0 notes correctly. Filter \"basic\" → 7/1/0/0 correct. So no.\n\nMaybe after a note is deleted/added while the Manage list is open in the background, then returning shows stale counts. Manage list can't stay open while adding... but we could use Undo? The Undo menu is only on deck list.\n\nHmm. Let's test the \"Add a new note type\" flow for a possible count bug: create \"qa_type\", check list. Also test renaming. Then delete.\n\nGiven time, the more important untested changed area is deck list expand/collapse. It requires subdecks. Let me create one and test, then delete.\n\nBut before that, I want to resolve the Card template editor menu question. Let me think again about whether cloze Add card type is a planted bug. Search memory of AnkiDroid source (CardTemplateEditor.java). I recall:\n\n```java\n@Override\npublic boolean onCreateOptionsMenu(Menu menu) {\n    getMenuInflater().inflate(R.menu.card_template_editor, menu);\n    return true;\n}\n\n@Override\npublic boolean onPrepareOptionsMenu(Menu menu) {\n    if (mModel == null) return false;\n    boolean isCloze = mModel.getModel().isCloze();\n    menu.findItem(R.id.action_add_card_type).setVisible(!isCloze);\n    menu.findItem(R.id.action_rename_card_type).setVisible(!isCloze);\n    menu.findItem(R.id.action_deck_override).setVisible(!isCloze);\n    ...\n}\n```\nHmm, but that would hide all three for cloze exactly as we observed except Add is visible. So the planted bug might be precisely that Add's visibility check was dropped/changed: \"menu's entries are now built the same way for every kind of note model\" — maybe they unified menu building and now Add is shown for cloze (bug). And Rename/Deck override remain hidden (correct for cloze per AnkiDroid design).\n\nActually, wait: Why would AnkiDroid hide Deck override for cloze? Hmm, maybe because cloze note types with deck override are... no, deck override is a notetype-level setting independent of cloze. But AnkiDroid's CardTemplateEditor \"Deck override (off)\" menu item lets you set deck override for the *current card template*? Hmm, \"Deck override\" is per-notetype, not per-template. If cloze is a different model type... no.\n\nHmm, maybe the hiding for cloze is because the deck override option is only for standard models? I doubt it.\n\nLet me examine \"Basic (type in the answer)\" menu (std, 1 template) for comparison: does it show Rename and Deck override? Probably yes.\n\nLet me instead check AnkiDroid actual release behavior from memory of using the app: In AnkiDroid 2.16, when editing a Cloze note type's card template, the overflow menu shows: \"Add card type\" (maybe greyed out?), \"Browser appearance\", \"Insert field\", \"Copy as Markdown\", \"Restore to default\". Hmm, I genuinely recall seeing \"Add card type\" in the cloze template editor... In Anki desktop, when editing a cloze notetype's template, the \"Options\" menu has \"Rename Card Type\" and \"Delete Card Type\" disabled? Actually in Anki 2.1 desktop, cloze notetypes *can* have multiple card templates? Let me recall Anki's manual: \"Cloze note types... only one card template\" — yes, in the Anki manual, \"Cloze note types only have a single card template\" or \"It is not possible to add additional card templates to a cloze note type\"? I'm fairly sure the desktop UI disables \"Add Card Type\" for cloze.\n\nGiven the change note explicitly mentions the menu entries built for every kind of note model, the planted bug likely is that the cloze/IO menu wrongly shows \"Add card type\" (or wrongly hides Rename/Deck override). We can report the Add card type as the observable defect with strong reasoning: it lets you create a second card type for a Cloze/Image Occlusion note type; the app itself says \"This will create 0 cards\", and that card can never be used. Expected: not offered.\n\nBut the developer might reject if AnkiDroid intentionally allows it (some versions allow adding templates to cloze which then are used for... hmm, Anki actually *does* allow multiple templates for cloze? Wait, I now recall that in newer Anki (2.1.50+), \"Add card type\" might be available for cloze notetypes too? Let me think about the backend: Anki's Notetype has `templates` list. For cloze notetypes, `card_requirements`... In Anki's Rust backend (`notetype/mod.rs`), there's `normalize_names`, and card generation: `CardGenContext::new` + `TimingContext`. For cloze notetype, cards are generated for each cloze number in the field, using template 0. If templates > 1, generation code: for cloze, `card_ord = cloze_number - 1`; with multiple templates, ord collides with template indices! Indeed in Anki, cloze note types MUST have exactly one template, else ord scheme breaks. Anki desktop enforces one template for cloze. Yes: \"Cloze note types can only have one card type\" — I'm now confident.\n\nSo Add card type for Cloze is a real bug. The dialog \"This will create 0 cards\" hints the app computes card count = 0 because cloze notes only generate cards from cloze numbers, so the new template would never be used. The app should not offer it.\n\nLet me confirm with Image Occlusion too: IO is a cloze-type notetype. Add card type there would be catastrophic. Its menu also shows Add. Same bug.\n\nI'll report this as a bug with element_ref from the Cloze card types menu ([0] Add card type). But my latest observation isn't that screen. I need to navigate back to Cloze card types menu and observe to get fresh element numbers. Let me do that, and also verify the dialog text again. If the dev rejects, fine; but I have reasonable confidence.\n\nActually, before that, let me examine the Deck override/Rename absence more. If Add is the bug, expected menu for cloze: Rename? AnkiDroid hides rename for cloze (since name \"Cloze\" fixed?) Hmm, on desktop you can rename cloze template? In desktop, the template name for cloze is displayed as \"Cloze\" and the rename option is available? I believe yes — you can rename card templates including cloze? Hmm, not sure.\n\nAnkiDroid