{"type": "thinking", "text": "Correct. Deck expand/collapse looks robust so far.\n\nHmm, but maybe the bug requires scrolling? With many decks, tapping an expander redraws only affected rows; rows below might not be rebound and show wrong content when they scroll into view. E.g., with many decks / long list, collapsing a top deck shifts rows up; rows below may duplicate or show stale expanded children. Our list has 5 rows total, all visible. Let's create enough decks/subdecks to require scrolling? That's heavy but doable: create several subdecks under French, then collapse to test rebinding of rows below the viewport. Since content fits on screen currently, no viewport recycling. Creating ~10 subdecks would exceed screen height and test recycling.\n\nBut this is a lot of data churn; and we need cleanup (delete decks). Could be worth it if the planted bug is about only redrawing affected rows (off-screen rows stale). Hmm.\n\nAlternatively, the bug might be simpler: after collapse/expand, the *deck counts* of other rows don't refresh (stale redraw). But we tested counts unchanged (they're static).\n\nWait — maybe the bug is about the effect of *adding* a note to a deck: deck list row counts update. The change \"a tap is now handled by redrawing only the affected deck's rows\" suggests performance optimization of expander taps; a common bug is that when you collapse a deck, the rows *below* are not shifted/redrawn, so you see stale/duplicate rows. Our observations show correct rows and positions.\n\nMaybe I haven't triggered the bug because the list is short. Let's think: the implementation probably uses a RecyclerView adapter and notifies item range changes; \"redraw only the affected deck's rows\" might mean it calls notifyItemRangeChanged on the parent's row range. If the changed-range count is wrong (e.g., using number of *visible* children vs all), rows after the affected deck might show wrong content. In our tests, everything after French (QASub/Deep/Spanish) updated properly. So maybe no bug there, or our test doesn't hit a specific condition.\n\nConsider a deck *below* French being collapsed: Spanish. Toggling Spanish (last row) — rows above unaffected. We did.\n\nConsider collapsing French when Spanish is expanded: we did (Spanish stayed expanded and rows moved). Correct.\n\nConsider expanding a subdeck QASub nested: did correctly.\n\nMaybe the bug involves the *counts_layout* (the \"Open the deck overview page...\" clickable) after redraw: tapping the counts area of a row that moved might open the wrong deck. We tested only when both collapsed. Let's test after expansion where rows moved: In current state French expanded, QASub expanded, Deep, Spanish. Tap Spanish's counts (element 17 at (978,675)) → Spanish overview. Then back, tap QASub counts (12 at 978,421) → should show QASub overview. Let's test to detect stale binding."}
