{"type": "thinking", "text": "Hmm! With 1 cloze note, adding a card type says \"This will create 1 card. Proceed?\" So it WOULD create a card from the new template for the existing cloze note?! That means in this AnkiDroid build, cloze note types support multiple templates and each template generates a card for each note? Interesting! That contradicts my assumption. If adding a template creates 1 card (for the 1 cloze note), then the feature works, and Add card type is legitimate.\n\nWait, but the cloze note had 1 cloze; adding a template creates a card for template 2. So cloze note types CAN have multiple templates and cards per template in this AnkiDroid/Anki version? Then Anki's model must support multiple templates for cloze (perhaps with ord = template index, and cards for cloze deletions are created from template 0 only? But it says 1 card created — template 2 card would presumably render `{{cloze:Text}}` with any cloze? That would be a duplicate card for the same cloze number but different ord. Maybe Anki does allow this in newer versions? Hmm.\n\nActually, in Anki's backend, cloze card generation: `CardGenContext` generates cards for each cloze number, with `template_idx`? I recall `card_ord` for cloze = cloze_number - 1, so multiple templates would collide... But maybe newer Anki uses ord = template_idx * ... no.\n\nRegardless — the app says adding a template to this cloze type will create 1 card, so it is a meaningful operation in this build. Thus \"Add card type\" for Cloze might be intended/functional. That weakens the bug claim. Since the dialog indicates it will create a card, the extra template is used. So don't report Add.\n\nHmm. Then what's the bug in the card template editor menu? Let's reconsider: Cloze menu lacks \"Rename card type\" and \"Deck override (off)\" compared to Basic. Perhaps the refactor \"entries built the same way for every kind of note model\" is exactly about this inconsistency: e.g., the menu for Cloze should have the same entries as Basic (Rename, Deck override). The phrase suggests unification—maybe the change aimed to build the menu identically for all types, and the bug is that some entries are missing for cloze/IO.\n\nLet's check: Does the cloze/IO menu include \"Deck override\"? In AnkiDroid, \"Deck override\" is a per-notetype setting; why would it be hidden for cloze? It shouldn't be—cloze note types can also have a deck override! Actually, hold on: In Anki, \"deck override\" (called \"Deck\" in notetype options) applies to notetypes; cloze notetypes can have it too. AnkiDroid hides it? I don't think so.\n\nAnd \"Rename card type\" for cloze: In Anki/AnkiDroid, you can rename any card template including cloze's. Hmm, AnkiDroid's cloze template name is \"Cloze\" and renaming... Let me test whether the app supports it elsewhere? If the menu lacks rename, no way to rename; maybe that's intended.\n\nHmm, actually maybe the planted bug is different in this area: maybe for standard models the menu lacks \"Add card type\" when it should have it, or image occlusion menu shows \"Insert field\" when it shouldn't, etc.\n\nLet me compare with what AnkiDroid typically shows in the card template editor for Cloze/Image Occlusion. I recall from AnkiDroid usage (2023, version 2.16): For a Cloze notetype, the \"Card types\" screen shows a single \"Cloze\" template and the overflow menu has:\n- \"Add card type\"? I think it's absent (grey).\n- \"Rename card type\"\n- \"Browser appearance\"\n- \"Deck override\"\n- \"Insert field\"\n- \"Copy as Markdown\"\n- \"Restore to default\"\n\nHmm. I'm going in circles. Let me test more empirically: if the menu item \"Deck override\" is hidden for cloze, but the cloze note type can still *have* a deck override (e.g., from Anki desktop), then the UI can't display/change it. Is there any other UI? No.\n\nMaybe we can find a functional defect related to menu entries: e.g., \"Insert field\" in cloze menu, when inserted, might not work? Or \"Restore to default\" for cloze? Let's test menu actions:\n- Insert field for cloze: tap → dialog with field list (Text, Back Extra) → pick → inserts \"{{Text}}\"? Should work.\n- Restore to default for cloze: resets template (would revert any edits; cancel).\n- Browser appearance: opens dialog (cancel).\n- Copy as Markdown: copies.\n\nHmm.\n\nWait, maybe the actual bug is that the menu is missing the \"Add card type\" for standard models once they have X templates? No.\n\nLet me look at the wording once more: \"Card template editor toolbar: the menu's entries are now built the same way for every kind of note model.\" — \"toolbar\" might refer to the editor's toolbar (top) not overflow menu. What's in the top toolbar? Navigate up, \"Card types\" title, deck name?, Save, Preview, More options. The \"menu's entries\" = overflow menu entries. \"built the same way\" = constructed by common code. So the bug is likely an entry incorrectly shown/hidden/mislabeled for a specific model kind. Our screenshot comparison found:\n- Basic: 7 entries\n- Basic (2 templates): 9 entries\n- Cloze: 5 entries (Add, Browser, Insert, Copy, Restore)\n- IO: 5 entries (same)\n\nIf the menu entries are built by common code with per-type visibility, what might be wrong? Consider: For cloze, \"Add card type\" *is* offered and works (dialog says 1 card). For cloze, \"Rename card type\" missing. But maybe the correct cloze menu should show \"Rename card type\" (since the card type is named \"Cloze\" and can be renamed). Hmm.\n\nWait — maybe the bug is on the *standard* side: the menu entries for \"Basic (and reversed card)\" include \"Reposition\" and \"Delete card type\" but those should perhaps be hidden for cloze only. Fine.\n\nCould the bug be the order of entries? \"the menu's entries are now built the same way\" — maybe order differs between models. Basic order: Add, Rename, Browser, Deck override, Insert field, Copy, Restore. Basic-reversed: Add, Reposition, Rename, Delete, Browser, Deck override, Insert, Copy, Restore. Cloze: Add, Browser, Insert, Copy, Restore. These orders are consistent with conditions. Nothing obviously out of order.\n\nMaybe there's a *duplicated* entry in a specific model's menu? Not seen.\n\nWhat about Image Occlusion: \"Add card type\" would create a card using the IO template? The IO template is special (HTML with image occlusion JS). Adding a second template for IO might create a plain card that references {{cloze:Occlusion}}—maybe valid functionally. Hmm.\n\nHold on, maybe the bug relates to the newer \"cards\" menu where for cloze models the card types are named \"Cloze\" and the menu should NOT show \"Add card type\" because the Anki backend *does* support only one template for cloze. But our test shows the app says \"This will create 1 card\" — that message is computed by counting cards generated after adding the template, using Anki's backend's `card_count_for_deck`? If the backend says 1 card, then maybe it does support. Unless the message is a naive local computation (notes count × templates?)... Actually in AnkiDroid, the dialog message \"This will create X cards. Proceed?\" comes from `mModel.getModel().getCardCountForDeck()`? Hmm, maybe it's computed as `noteCount` (count of notes of this model in the collection?) — Wait, for the empty Cloze it said 0 cards; after adding 1 cloze note it says 1 card. For a standard model with 2 templates and 2 notes, adding a template would create 2 cards (one per note). The dialog for Cloze with 1 note says 1 card — consistent with \"notes × 1 new template = 1\". So the app *expects* the new template to create a card per note; and for a cloze note with 1 cloze this may be true. So cloze multi-template is supported here? Weird but possible in recent Anki (maybe they changed cloze ord to be per-template?).\n\nHmm wait, maybe Anki's backend generates cloze cards as (template, cloze_number) pairs; ord = template_idx * 1000 + cloze? I'm not sure. Actually I recall in Anki's Rust: `for template_idx in 0..nt.templates.len() { for cloze_idx in ... }`? There is code `let card_ord = if nt.is_cloze() { template_idx * ... }`. Hmm, maybe in newer Anki, cloze cards use ord = cloze_number - 1 + template_idx? Not sure.\n\nSince the dialog says 1 card will be created, the feature is likely functional; don't report Add.\n\nBut then what's the menu bug? Maybe th", "truncated": true}
