{"type": "thinking", "text": "Confirmed: Cloze now has two card types: \"Cloze\" and \"Card 2\". The Card 2 template is stored but generates no cards. This is the bug: the card template editor offers \"Add card type\" for Cloze (and Image Occlusion) note models, and even claims it will create a card, but cloze cards are generated per cloze deletion, so the extra template never produces cards.\n\nWait, but is it possible the card will be generated only for *newly added* cloze notes (i.e., existing notes' cards not regenerated)? The dialog said it would create 1 card for existing note(s) — implying a rebuild. Hmm, but maybe AnkiDroid updates card count for existing notes asynchronously and deck list didn't refresh? Let's verify by checking the *Browser* for the note's cards, or by adding a NEW cloze note now and seeing if 2 cards are added. If new cloze notes generate cards for both templates, then Card 2 works for new notes but existing notes weren't updated (ancestor bug different). Let's test:\n\nAdd a new cloze note \"{{c1::qa_cloze2}}\" in QASub. If \"2 cards added\" → template works for new notes; then the dialog's promise was about existing note regeneration, which didn't happen → bug = existing notes' cards not rebuilt? Hmm, but actually, does AnkiDroid rebuild cards when adding a template? On desktop, adding a card type triggers \"This will create N cards\" and generates them for all notes. If it created 0, that's a bug. Either way there's a bug.\n\nBut wait, is it possible the deck list count didn't refresh due to the redraw-only optimization? No, that's expander taps. The counts are recomputed on resume.\n\nLet me test adding a new cloze note to see \"cards added\". This requires another note (we'll delete both). Do it.\n\nActually, simpler check: open the Card Browser and search for the qa_cloze note; the browser shows cards count via \"cards\" column? Let's use deck overview total cards: QASub total 3 (after template add) vs expected 4. That's already evidence existing note didn't get a new card.\n\nLet me test new note quickly: Add > Cloze > {{c1::qa_cloze2}} > save; snackbar tells 1 or 2. Let's do it.\n\nBack twice to deck list, Add, select Cloze, deck QASub, type, save."}
