fore adding Card 2 template; after adding the template to Cloze (1 note), French stayed 8. Then I added qa_cloze2 note with 2 templates → French went 9; Card browser shows QASub 4 cards: qa_subnote 2 + qa_cloze 1 + qa_cloze2 1 = 4. So neither the existing note's new-template card nor the new note's second-template card exists. Total cards would be 6 if working. So no.\n\nCould it be that the browser view I'm seeing is filtered by the current deck (French::QASub) and the Card 2 cards are in another deck (e.g., Default due to unknown template deck override)? Adding a template might create cards in the \"Default\" deck? But notes have deck French::QASub; cards inherit note deck unless overridden. The template \"Card 2\" deck override is off. Hmm, but maybe new cards from a newly added template land in the *home deck* (Default)? Unlikely.\n\nLet me check the browser for all decks. The toolbar says \"French::QASub 4 cards shown\" — maybe deck filter applied. Could search for \"qa_cloze\" globally? Use Search button with \"qa_cloze\". Actually, browser Search filters within current deck? The toolbar deck selection is French::QASub. There might be a card in Default. Let's search \"qa_cloze\" across all decks by changing deck to \"All decks\"? In AnkiDroid browser, the deck filter can be changed via toolbar deck name. Alternatively, search `qa_cloze` and see results; the search is usually global unless deck filter. The toolbar says deck \"French::QASub\", so it's filtered.\n\nLet me use Search action (3) and type \"qa_cloze\"; if filtered by deck, still 2 notes. Hmm.\n\nAlternatively, check the note editor's \"Cards: Cloze, Card 2\" button — tapping it may show the list of cards for that note (with counts) — for the saved qa_cloze2 note. In the Add screen, the button is just a label; tapping may show a dialog \"Card types\" list? Let's test on a new note (no saved). But for the saved note, we can open from browser: tap note row → opens card browser editing? Actually tapping