{"type": "thinking", "text": "Interesting! Trying to delete Card 2 from the Cloze note type gives \"Cannot delete card type — Deleting this card type will leave some notes without any cards.\" Wait, this means the Cloze notes HAVE cards that use Card 2?! If Card 2 had no cards, deleting it wouldn't leave notes without cards. Hmm! Maybe the cloze notes DO have cards on Card 2 template that we didn't see? But the browser showed only Cloze 1 cards. Hmm.\n\nWait, maybe the message is generic: \"Deleting this card type will leave some notes without any cards\" because deleting *any* card type except the only one... For cloze, removing Card 2 leaves only Cloze template, which is fine. But Anki's backend logic: if a note would lose all its cards after deletion, block. For the 2 cloze notes, they have Cloze 1 cards from template 0, so deleting template 1 should be safe. Unless... the cloze notes' only cards are on template 1?? The browser showed \"Cloze 1\" as card type for both cloze notes. Hmm.\n\nHmm, wait: maybe the browser's \"Card Type\" column for cloze cards shows \"Cloze 1\" (cloze number) regardless of template? And perhaps the actual card ord for the extra template is used? Confusing.\n\nIf deleting is blocked because notes would be left without cards, maybe the situation is the reverse of what I thought: the *Card 2* template is actually the one generating the cards for these cloze notes, and the \"Cloze\" template 0 is unused?! How? Let's think: When I added Card 2 to the Cloze type, maybe AnkiDroid re-assigned the cloze notes' cards to the new template (Card 2) — because Anki's cloze card generation uses the *last* template? That seems odd.\n\nActually! Maybe this is the clue to the real seeded bug: The new card type was created with template content \"{{cloze:Text}}<br>\\n{{Back Extra}}\" and is named \"Card 2\". For cloze notetypes, cards are generated per cloze number, and the *ord* encodes the template? Hmm.\n\nWait, maybe the deletion is blocked not because of Card 2's cards, but because Anki's backend refuses to delete a card type from a cloze notetype when there are notes at all (since cloze cards' ord may map to templates in a way where no template is safe). Hmm.\n\nLet's check the Card Browser's card type labels: they said \"Cloze 1\". With two templates, maybe AnkiDroid labels cloze card types as \"Cloze 1\"/\"Card 2\"? The card ord for a cloze card might be `cloze_number - 1` = 0 for c1, which maps to template 0 (\"Cloze\"). So the cards are template 0. Deleting template 1 should be safe. Unless the backend's check is simplistic: \"if (notes_with_only_this_template...)\": maybe it checks cards where ord == templateIndex... For cloze, ord 0 < templates.len() so cards with ord 0 are on both templates? Hmm.\n\nThis is a rabbit hole. The important thing: we now cannot delete Card 2 via the UI (blocked!). So my cleanup path is blocked. We could use Undo \"Update Note Type\" from the deck list to revert the note type change! The Undo menu showed \"Undo Update Note Type\" earlier — but after adding notes since then, the undo history may have newer actions (Add Note qa_cloze2). Undo stack: Add Note qa_cloze2 is most recent, then Update Note Type. We could undo twice: undo Add Note (removes qa_cloze2), then undo Update Note Type (removes Card 2 template). That would restore the Cloze type. Let's do that.\n\nBut first dismiss this dialog (OK) and back out. Then deck list → overflow → Undo Add Note (removes qa_cloze2), then Undo Update Note Type (reverts template). Then also undo earlier Add Note qa_cloze? Order: undo history: add qa_cloze2, update note type, add qa_cloze, add qa_subnote, add qa_rev1... Actually the \"Update Note Type\" was done after adding qa_cloze, and then qa_cloze2 was added after. So undo stack (newest first): Add qa_cloze2, Update Note Type, Add qa_cloze, Add qa_subnote, Add qa_rev1, Unselect Deck, ... So undo twice removes qa_cloze2 and the template update. Then I can undo more to remove qa_cloze, qa_subnote, qa_rev1 (but each undo is a separate menu action). That's efficient cleanup! But careful: the undo stack might be cleared/limited due to closing collection? It persists in the session. Let's use it.\n\nFirst OK dialog."}
